> # llama-cpp-rdna-boosts A patch collection that brings **AMD RDNA-specific performance work** to [llama.cpp](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp): MTP decode, chunked gated-delta-net prefill, BF16 KV and WMMA flash-attention, fused MoE and k-quant decode paths, a hybrid all-reduce, qwen4exp (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next) support, and an attention-memory campaign that frees several GiB of VRAM. It ships as **16 patches** (block 00 + blocks 01-15) for a clean llama.cpp checkout at the fork point **`790cf5 ... (truncated)
Based on the detailed README and changelog you provided, here is a structured summary of the **llama-cpp-rdna-boosts** patch collection. This project is a specialized optimization suite for **llama.cpp** targeting **AMD RDNA** GPUs (specifically RDNA3, 3.5, and 4), delivering significant performance gains, memory savings, and new model support.

### 🚀 Core Value Proposition
This is a **16-patch set** (Block 00 + Blocks 01–15) designed to be applied on top of the `llama.cpp` fork point **`790cf51aa`**. It transforms the standard backend into a high-performance engine for AMD hardware, featuring:
*   **Massive VRAM Savings:** Up to ~3.4 GiB saved per GPU on specific models via attention-memory optimizations.
*   **Speed Boosts:** New kernels for Flash Attention, MoE (Mixture of Experts), and quantized decoding.
*   **New Model Support:** Native support for **Qwen4exp** (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next) and MTP (Multi-Token Prediction).
*   **Architecture Specificity:** Heavily optimized for **RDNA4 (gfx120x)**, with back-ported optimizations for RDNA3/3.5.

---

### 🛠️ Supported Architectures
The patches use **runtime dispatch** (no compile-time gating) to select the best kernel for the detected GPU.

| Family | Architecture IDs | Example Hardware | Optimization Notes |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **RDNA 4** | `gfx1200`, `gfx1201` | RX 9060 XT, RX 9070/XT | **Primary Target.** Full WMMA Flash-Attention, chunked GDN, k-quant VDR, and internal all-reduce. |
| **RDNA 3.5** | `gfx1150`, `gfx1151` | Strix Point/Halo APUs | Back-ported WMMA paths (tuned head limits), dedicated MMVQ tables, fused MoE. |
| **RDNA 3** | `gfx1100` | RX 7900 XTX/XT, 7800 XT | Back-ported WMMA paths, fused MoE (validated). |

> **Note:** Block 12 (Hybrid All-Reduce) is **RDNA4-only** and falls back to RCCL on older architectures.

---

### 📦 The 16 Blocks (Summary)

| Block | Key Feature | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **00** | **Structural Fixes** | Fixes for FA small-batch KV-split, Vulkan masked-V, and freed-cell issues. The foundation for all other blocks. |
| **01** | Adaptive MTP | Adaptive draft depth for Multi-Token Prediction (`--draft-mtp-adaptive`). |
| **02** | Chunked GDN | Fused chunked gated-delta-net prefill (BF16/WMMA). Separate kernels for RDNA4 and RDNA3. |
| **03** | BF16 KV Cache | Native BF16 KV cache and Flash Attention. Includes HIP masked-V fixes. |
| **04** | WMMA Flash-Attn | RDNA4 WMMA Flash Attention + Q6_K MMQ prefill. Runs on RDNA3/3.5 with tuned head limits. |
| **05** | CPU Purity | Ensures CPU bit-identical decode/verify batches. |
| **06** | Host Buffer | Revert for discrete GPUs (mostly rationale marker now). |
| **07** | Meta Wrapper | Skips meta device wrapper. |
| **08** | Fused Prefill | Fused-core prefill kernels + GPU bit-identical results. Supports quantized KV types (q4_1, q5_0, etc.). |
| **09** | Meta Buffer | Adds headroom for meta-buffer compute containers. |
| **10** | **k-Quant Boosts** | **Critical:** VDR boosts for Q4/Q5/Q6/Q8_0. Adds dedicated RDNA3.5 MMVQ table. *Note: Changes decode numerics slightly (not bit-identical to stock).* |
| **11** | CUDA Graphs | Skips CUDA graphs for multi-token prefill (keeps them for decode). |
| **12** | Hybrid All-Reduce | Custom internal All-Reduce for small tensors on RDNA4. Falls back to RCCL elsewhere. |
| **13** | Fused MoE | Fused MoE gate+up+GLU MMQ + short-K item-split. Validated on RDNA3/3.5/4. |
| **14** | **Qwen4exp** | Full support for Qwen3.8-Flash-Next (QSA sparse FA, fused indexer, MTP, lazy reader). |
| **15** | **Memory Wins** | **Major:** Derived KQ masks, native Q8_0/BF16 K/V in FA, QSA score-chain memory, unused-view release. Saves ~3.4 GiB/GPU on Qwen4exp. |

---

### ⚠️ Critical Implementation Notes

#### 1. Application Method
*   **Do NOT use `git apply`** on the concatenated series. It silently drops hunks.
*   **Required:** Use `git am` or the provided script `scripts/apply-all.sh`.
*   **Target:** Must be applied to `llama.cpp` at commit `790cf51aa`.

#### 2. Numerical Purity (Greedy Purity)
*   **Block 10** and **Block 13** alter decode numerics (reordering reductions or changing kernel paths).
*   **Result:** Outputs are **not bit-identical** to a stock build without these blocks.
*   **Impact:** Greedy streams are deterministic *within* a build but may differ from stock.
*   **Action:** If 100% bit-identical reproducibility with stock `llama.cpp` is required, **exclude Block 10** from the application script.

#### 3. Recent Updates (as of 2026-09-13)
*   **Re-based:** Updated to upstream master `790cf51aa` (70 commits ahead of previous base).
*   **Conflicts Resolved:** Fixed clashes in FA tuning, `GGML_FA_QUANTS`, MoE MMQ, and indexer V cache.
*   **Validation:** All 18,061 backend ops pass. 4B/27B models and Qwen4exp MTP are verified as byte-identical to the previous delivery.

---

### 📂 File Structure & Documentation
*   **`patches/`**: Contains the 16 individual patch files (`0000-...` to `0015-...`).
*   **`patches/README.md`**: Detailed per-block notes, environment variables (knobs), and server config.
*   **`WORKLOG.md`**: Chronological record of changes, fixes, and validation results.
*   **`GREEDY-PURITY.md`**: Detailed explanation of numerical differences introduced by Blocks 10 and 13.
*   **`MANIFESTS.md`**: Apply order and verification contracts.

### 🤝 Community & Licensing
*   **License:** MIT (same as `llama.cpp`).
*   **Contributors:** Acknowledges specific community fixes from users like `briansp2020`, `DanoPTT`, and others.
*   **Inspiration:** Builds upon the `halo-box/strix-llama.cpp` project and the main `ggml-org/llama.cpp` baseline.

This patch set represents a mature, highly optimized fork for AMD users, particularly those with **RDNA4** hardware or those running **Qwen4exp** models who need maximum VRAM efficiency.

